            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25681",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/net/html: golang.org/x/net/html: Arbitrary code execution via Cross-Site Scripting"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Parsing arbitrary HTML which is then rendered using Render can result in an unexpected HTML tree. This can be leveraged to execute XSS attacks in applications that attempt to sanitize input HTML before rendering."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25681",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-25681\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nFixed Version: 0.55.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-25681](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25681)\nParsing arbitrary HTML which is then rendered using Render can result in an unexpected HTML tree. This can be leveraged to execute XSS attacks in applications that attempt to sanitize input HTML before rendering.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-25681**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|golang.org/x/net|0.55.0|[CVE-2026-25681](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25681)|\n\nParsing arbitrary HTML which is then rendered using Render can result in an unexpected HTML tree. This can be leveraged to execute XSS attacks in applications that attempt to sanitize input HTML before rendering."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
